# LED board fit (s3.1.25)

Resume: `@board-fit$` / `$led-fit$`.

Modules: `floqr-board-fit.js` → `window.FLOQRBoardFit` (also `module.exports` for tests) and `floqr-board-frame.js` → `window.FLOQRBoardFrame`. Tests: `functions/board-fit.test.js`, `functions/display-text-fit.test.js`. `display-app.js` keeps a fallback path for every call so it still works on pages that do not load the modules (local QA pages).

## A — Board size: Firestore wins

`display-app.js` `mergeLiveVenue(packagedLoc, live)` → `FLOQRBoardFit.mergeVenueForDisplay`, then `FLOQRScreenDatapoints.applyVenue`.

| Field | Rule |
|---|---|
| `primaryDisplayScreenFormatId` | live `primaryDisplayScreenFormatId` → live `displayType` → live `screenFormatId` → packaged (same order) |
| `secondaryDisplayScreenFormatId` | live → packaged → merged primary |
| `displayScreenFormatIds` | live list when non-empty, else packaged (no union) |
| `VenueSupports96x48/64x48/64x32` | live when explicit `0|1`, else packaged when explicit, else unset |
| everything else | `{...packaged, ...live}` |

Unchanged semantics kept in `mergeLiveVenue`: `displayFooterBrand` (live → packaged → "FLOQR ShoutOut"), `ledPanel`, `approvedDisplayIps` (live or `[]`), `displayIpRestrictionEnabled === true`, `displayTokenRequired`. `FLOQRBoardFit.effectiveBoardSize` reports `{formatId, source: firestore|packaged|default}` for diagnostics.

## B — Only approved/live content renders

`isRenderableLiveContent(data)` → `FLOQRBoardFit.liveContentDecision(data) === "live"`: status `approved` or `live` **and** non-blank `mainText` or a `mediaUrl`. Any other status (pending, rejected, played, expired, preview, default, empty) shows the idle club board (`defaultClubDisplayPayload`). The live snapshot keeps the literal `const isIdleDoc = !doc.exists || isIdlePayload(payload) || …` — `ai-diagnostics-service.js` greps for it.

Expiry (`liveContentExpiresMillis` → `FLOQRBoardFit.liveExpiryMillis`), first match wins:

1. `expiresAt` / `liveUntil` / `playedUntil`
2. `approvedAt` + `displayDurationSeconds` (default 600)
3. `updatedAt` / `createdAt` + duration
4. first-seen + duration — first-seen persisted in `localStorage["floqr.liveFirstSeen.<liveContentDocId>"]` keyed by `livePlaybackKey`, so a Xibo reload does not restart the clock.

On expiry the board shows the idle board and remembers `expiredLiveKey` so the same doc does not replay.

## E — Text fit

- Words are never split (`pushWrapped` puts an over-long word on its own row; `packAllWordsIntoRows` / `packWordsWithoutSplitting` grow the per-row budget instead of slicing) and never dropped: if the line-break pass would drop words, all words are repacked. The template character cap (`maxMainCharacters`) still applies, via `wholeWordSlice` — it ends at the last whole word, never mid-word.
- Classic (`.classic-board-lines > b`) and text-overlay (`.text-overlay-lines > b`) rows render as `<b style="--fit-size…"><span class="board-fit-run">…</span></b>`. `FLOQRBoardFit.scheduleFit(canvas)` runs at the end of `render` (and the jersey branch) on paint, next frames, `document.fonts.ready`, and ResizeObserver.
- Each row keeps its designed `--fit-size`. Only a row whose run would exceed the row minus the safe margin (**4 % each side horizontally, 6 % vertically**) gets an inline `font-size: Npx !important`. Floor `MIN_SCALE` 0.3 of the designed size.
- `fitDisplayMessageLines` (full/split templates) binary-searches against the same safe width/height.
- Identity pill `.classic-identity-shell strong` shrinks instead of ellipsis (`text-overflow: clip` once fitted).
- Wider boards fit more naturally because the measurement is in real pixels.

## F — Idle CTA fit (s3.1.40)

**Owner principle (Oct 13 2026): visibility first — biggest font wins.** Start from the biggest size the board can hold, try every row arrangement at that size, and step down to the next size only when no arrangement fits (whole words, nothing cut, safe margins). All rows share that one size. Apply the same principle to any future board text fit.

Applies **only** to the idle / default classic board (`isIdlePayload`: `status: default` or `idleCta`, template `blackwhite`, `classic-bw-idle`). Live patron ShoutOuts keep E above, the 48-char cap and `classicFitStyle` per-row sizing.

- **No cap.** `display-app.js` skips the classic `mainSource.slice(0, mainLimit + lineCount - 1)` and the `classicBoardRows` / `maxMainCharacters` path for idle. `idleBoardText` uppercases, collapses whitespace, and only guards against junk at `FLOQRBoardFit.IDLE_MAX_GLYPHS` (160, whole words). Before s3.1.40 the 64×32 cap (30) turned Heist into `USE / SHOUTOUT @ / HEIST`.
- **Rows.** `FLOQRBoardFit.rankIdleRows(text, safeW, safeH)`: tokens with `@` glued to the previous word (`SHOUTOUT @` never splits); every contiguous split into ≤ `IDLE_MAX_ROWS` (5) rows (greedy min-max fallback above 12 tokens); score = estimated uniform px (`0.52em`/glyph, `IDLE_LINE_EM` 0.95/row) × 0.93 if the club name does not start a row × 0.96 per extra row the club name spans; ties → most balanced. `pickIdleRows` = top entry (render-time first paint).
- **One size.** Host `<span class="classic-board-lines" data-idle-fit="1" data-idle-text="…">`, every row gets the same `--fit-size`. `fitBoard` sends idle hosts to `fitIdleHost` (per-row `fitRows` skips them): measure the top 4 ranked splits at 100px in the real box, keep the largest `px × preference`, apply that px to **every** row (inline `!important`), then step down until each run fits its row cell (`max(runHeight, 0.95·px) ≤ cellH`, width ≤ host). Stamps `data-idle-fit-px`. Re-runs on ResizeObserver / fonts.ready, so a Xibo viewport change re-packs.
- **Safe area.** `display.css` insets the idle host to 92% × 88% (= SAFE_X 4% / SAFE_Y 6%) so fitting inside the host is fitting inside the safe area. The ruled backdrop uses `calc(100% / var(--board-lines,3))`; `display-app.js` / `setIdleRows` set `--board-lines` on `#displayMain` to the row count.
- **Display 2** idle is the SupRstar screen (`renderSuprstarIdleScreen`), not this board. s3.1.40 adds a `max-height:260px` rule so the logo, both lines and the note stay on a 64×32 (416×208) board; the copy column is `width:100%` of the centre with `text-wrap:balance`.
- QA: `reports/idle-fit-s3-1-40/idle-qa.mjs <label> <base>` (CDP, display + display2 × default / Zebbies / Heist / Aurelia × 64×32 / 64×48 / 96×48 / 1920×1080). Test: `functions/idle-board-fit.test.js`.

## Preview fidelity

- `FLOQRBoardFrame.mount(iframe, formatId, {maxHeight})` wraps the iframe in `.floqr-board-frame`, sizes the iframe to the board's native pixels (`FLOQR_DISPLAY_FORMATS[id].pixelWidth/pixelHeight`: 96×48 = 624×312, 64×48 = 416×312, 64×32 = 416×208) and CSS-transform scales it to the host (ResizeObserver). `vw`/`px` clamps and `@media(max-width:760px)` inside display.css therefore behave exactly as on the LED.
- Used by `patron-app.js` `updatePreview` (`#previewFrame`), `floqr-template-preview.js` (template preview modal), and Club Admin `#liveFrame` (packaged primary size).
- `display-app.js` preview mode (`isUrlPreviewMode`): `paintUrlPreviewNow()` paints from packaged data at once, then `hydrateUrlPreviewFromFirestore()` loads Firestore templates + venue (same `mergeLiveVenue`) and re-renders the last payload given to `window.renderShoutOutDisplay` (or rebuilds the URL payload). Preview never calls Display Security.
- Preview URLs still never carry `?v=`; Xibo URLs stay `display.html?location=` / `display2.html?location=`.

## Safe render (s3.1.39)

Origin: preview mode needs no auth, so `display.html?location=…&preview=1&template=zebbiesFootballTeamIntro&backgroundUrl=x><b id=floqrprobe>` injected markup on the Pages origin (the Firebase session lives there). Patron-set fields also reached public `liveContent` through Club Admin approve, and the queue Preview link opened the patron's URL on the admin's origin.

Module: `floqr-safe-render.js` → `window.FLOQRSafeRender` (also `module.exports`). Load it **before** `display-app.js`, `floqr-template-preview.js` and `admin-app.js`. Without it, `display-app.js` fails closed (no URL / color / gradient from data reaches the board).

| API | Contract |
|---|---|
| `escapeHtml(v)` | `& < > " ' \`` |
| `safeUrl(v, {allowBlob, allowDataImage})` | absolute `http(s)` (no credentials, normalized `href`) or same-origin `images/…` (no `..`); opt-in `blob:http(s)://` and raster base64 `data:image/png|jpeg|gif|webp|avif`. Everything else (`javascript:`, `data:text`, SVG data, `//host`, control chars, >2048) → `""` |
| `cssUrl(v, opts)` | `url("…")` with `" ' ( ) \ < >` and whitespace percent-encoded, or `""` |
| `safeColor(v, fallback)` | hex 3/4/6/8, `rgb/rgba/hsl/hsla(numbers)`, or a 3–20 letter name |
| `safeGradient(v, fallback)` | `linear-gradient(...)` charset only, ≤400, balanced parens, no `url( var( attr( env( expression image-set` |
| `styleAttr(decls)` | joins with `;` and HTML-escapes the whole value |

Every innerHTML / style sink in `display-app.js` (background layer, frame overlay, Football Intro stage + player media, split media, jersey colors, Heist logo) uses these. `floqr-template-preview.js` escapes Firestore `screenFormatIds`. Patron composer sanitizes football background / media inputs and the jersey mini preview. Club Admin approve (`boardUrl` / `boardColor` / `boardTeamMembers`) vets every render field before writing `liveContent`; the queue Preview link has `rel="noopener"`.

Rules (`firestore.rules` `validBoardRenderFields`): patron shoutout create (paid + free), owner edit, and every `liveContent` create/update must pass the same URL / color / gradient allowlists (RE2 mirrors of the helper). Rules cannot check list elements (`teamMembers`) — render + approve sanitize those. Club manager updates on `shoutouts` are not validated so admins can still reject bad docs.

Test: `functions/display-safe-render.test.js` (fake-DOM render of `display-app.js` with the probe + `"`, `)`, `</style>`, `javascript:`, newline variants; asserts no injected tag/attribute and quoted-safe CSS).

## Intentionally untouched

- **C:** `classicFitStyle` compact / primary-format logic (Display 2 sizing on `64x32` uses `loc.primaryDisplayScreenFormatId`). Guarded by a test in `board-fit.test.js`.
- **D:** display health / error diagnostics.

## Known limits

- The neon / full template sub line (`#displaySub`) and @handles are capped by `maxSubCharacters` / handle caps before render; that is a data cap, not CSS clipping. The composer enforces the same caps.
- Club Admin `#liveFrame` sizes from the packaged venue row (admin-app does not merge Firestore there yet).
